//! check: run(exit=0)
//! phase: run
//! conforms: std.list
//!
//! THE cross-implementation triage case the sprint contract names, and
//! it does NOT agree at these pins (finding F-0014):
//!
//! - wolfc REJECTS it statically — `fail(E1001)`, because `for x in xs`
//!   moves `xs` and `xs.push` then reads a moved place. A rejection is a
//!   fine answer; it is not the `exclusivity` trap `[conf.trap.map]`
//!   would predict, and it arrives through the reads-as-moves lens
//!   (F-0005) rather than a container-exclusivity rule.
//! - lupin RUNS it to completion, silently, with no trap at all — the
//!   under-enforcement half of the divergence.
//!
//! The directive therefore records the LUPIN behavior (run, exit 0) and
//! the ledger records wolfc's `fail(E1001)`: the file exists so the
//! divergence has a home in CI until one of the two moves.

fn main() -> !int {
    var xs = List[int]()
    xs.push(1)
    xs.push(2)
    for x in xs {
        xs.push(x)
    }
    0
}
